    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0638" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg550"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 416.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring No. 413 of March 26, instant, I
                    beg to state that I have received, and herewith inclose, the report of the
                    United <pb facs="0639" n="551" xml:id="pg551"/> States consul at Smyrna, in the
                    matter of the refusal of the Turkish authorities to permit Rev. Mr. Bartlett to
                    purchase the property in which he lives.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>




